== Notes ==
* Defeating Mom for the first time changes the current [[Savefile Images|savefile's image]] and will allow unlocks to be obtained with mods enabled.
* The 'Stats' section of the menu keeps a tally of "Mom kills". However, this refers to how many times you've defeated Mom completely, as in, how many times you've killed {{e|Mom's Heart}}, not just Mom.
* Using {{i|The Bible}} or {{p|XV - The Devil?}} during the Mom boss fight kills her instantly and unlocks {{i|The Halo}}.
* Using {{p|II - The High Priestess}} during the fight with Mom results in Isaac being targeted instead of the enemy with the highest health. However, the stomp can still damage Mom.
* {{dlc|nr}} Mom's stomp attack counts as a bomb; this means Isaac can be immune to it with {{i|Pyromaniac}} or {{i|Host Hat}}.
** {{dlc|nr}} With {{i|Pyromaniac}}, Isaac can be healed when stomped.
** {{dlc|nr}} Red Champion Mom is greatly negated with {{i|Pyromaniac}} or {{i|Host Hat}}.
** {{dlc|r}} Mom's stomp attack now deals contact damage, causing immunity to explosions to no longer avoid damage from the stomp.
* {{i|The Polaroid}} will always spawn on the left pedestal and {{i|The Negative}} is always on the right.

== Trivia ==
* In Mom's entry in the bestiary, her "kills" value will never increase. It is unclear if this is a lore implication or a bug.
* In [https://foursouls.com/cards/g2-credit_card/ The Binding of Isaac: Four Souls rendition] of [[Credit Card]], the name "Magdalene O. Moriah" can be seen carved in the credit card. The name was reused on [https://twitter.com/edmundmcmillen/status/1087851233585418241 the Four Souls+ rendition] of {{I|Divorce Papers}}. [[Edmund McMillen|Edmund]] has confirmed that this is indeed Mom's full name.
** The initials spell out "M.O.M.".
** {{dlc|r}} This is further confirmed in-game during the background conversation during the [[Ascent]], where Dad calls Mom "Maggy" as he tells her to shut up.
** The last name "Moriah" is likely a reference to the [[wikipedia:Moriah|biblical location of the same name]]. In the Bible, it is said that Moriah is where Abraham almost sacrificed his son before God sent an angel to stop his hand.
** The playable character {{c|Magdalene}} shares a first name with Mom, but whether or not the two of them have connections remains yet to be known.
* According to Edmund, the [https://twitter.com/edmundmcmillen/status/1217899733005455361?s=21 occupations of Mom and Dad] are stay-at-home mom and handyman respectively.
* Mom is voiced by '''Carla Kihlstedt'''.
* The battle theme for this boss is "Matricide", a term for the killing of one's own mother.
* Mom appeared in the original ''The Binding of Isaac.''
** In the original, Mom's voice was provided by '''Michelle Schroeder-Lowrey''', an associate of Jordan Fehr, the sound designer.
** Unlike in ''Rebirth'', Mom would shout "Isaac!" whenever she exposed her eye.
** The battle theme in the original game was "Thine Wrath..."
* Using {{i|The Bible}} and killing Mom instantly is a reference to how a bible hits her head in the epilogue of the game, knocking her out or killing her.
* Mom's eye appearing out of the doors could represent Mom's peeping in Isaac's room to check on him.
* Mom constantly screaming "Isaac" seems to suggest how Mom was desperately trying to find her son.
* Mom is the only final boss that has Champion variants.
* During the versus screen, the "Isaac!" line from Mom can be heard, despite the battle not starting yet. She is one of {{dlc|nr}} seven/{{dlc|r}} five bosses that can be heard during the versus screen; the other {{dlc|nr}} six/{{dlc|r}} four are {{e|Big Horn}}, {{e|The Stain}}, {{e|The Forsaken}}, {{dlc|nr}} {{e|Mom's Heart}}, {{dlc|nr}} {{e|It Lives!}}, and {{e|Mother}}.
* The skirt she wears on her in-game sprite is difficult to see in regular play, as her leg extends past the screen. Using the {{i|Dataminer}} or the {{i|Meat Cleaver}} can make the skirt visible.
** {{dlc|a+}} Delirium's Mom form appears to wear a pile of flesh and organs rather than a skirt.
* A disembodied version of Mom's leg stomp attack can be summoned as part of the effects of {{p|II - The High Priestess}}, {{t|Mom's Toenail}}, {{i|Broken Shovel 1}}, and {{p|II - The High Priestess?}}.
* {{dlc|a+}} Prior to [[Booster Packs#Booster Pack #5|Booster Pack #5]], Globins spawned by Mom could turn into {{e|Dank Globin}}s if she was fought in Dank Depths.
* {{dlc+|r}} When she is fought in the {{s|Mausoleum}}, her leg appears to be in a much more sickly state, with many varicose veins lining it.{{dlc-}}
** Her hand also has a unique updated sprite, despite the fact that she never uses it in this fight.
* {{e|Mother}} could be considered as her posthumous version.
* Mom later made appearances in The Legend of Bumbo and Mewgenics, two other games by Edmund.

